  "story": {
    "wol": "James Woolstencroft and Alice Collier lived around Radcliffe, Lancashire. Their son George brought the family to Pennsylvania by 1858. Four generations later, Irvin Jr. was drafted in 1943, married Mary Nagy and settled in North Versailles.",
    "nag": "Kalman Nagy came from Milota in Hungary's far northeast. He and Isabelle Toth settled in McKeesport, where their daughter Mary was born in 1917.",
    "spe": "Philip Henry Specht, born in Germany, married Anna Deitman, daughter of an immigrant from Rottleben, Thuringia. Their son Ed was born in Punxsutawney and spent his working life at Westinghouse in East Pittsburgh.",
    "mor": "Peter Mortelette arrived from Charleroi, Belgium, in 1892 and settled in McDonald, a Belgian coal and glass town. His son Jules married Julia Jiannino, daughter of an Italian immigrant, and raised Esther beside the Westinghouse works.",
    "meet": "Ed Specht worked at Westinghouse in East Pittsburgh, where Esther grew up. A generation later Rod grew up in North Versailles and Yvonne in Murrysville, about 10 miles apart."
  },
